WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.310
Joe: From portion sizes to exclusives,

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.200
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:09.090
between McDonald's in the
US, UK, Japan, and India.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.645
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.870
In the US, our McDonald's
sodas come in three sizes.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:19.703
Small.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:21.473
Medium.

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:23.400
This is what a medium drink looks like.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.813
Japan's large.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.481
Regular, medium, and large.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.970
Our chicken McNuggets come in four, six,

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.695
10, 20,

00:00:37.695 --> 00:00:39.630
or 40-piece.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.580
So, with our McNuggets in the UK,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.870
the default adult sizes on
the menu are a box of six.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:46.920
Six pieces.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.180
Harry: A box of nine.
Nikhil: Nine pieces.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.650
Harry: Or 20.
Nikhil: And 20 pieces.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.260
They gave it to us in
two boxes of 10 each.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.307
In Japan, our chicken
McNuggets come in five

00:00:55.307 --> 00:00:56.742
and 15 pieces.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.750
In the US, you can get
your fries in four sizes.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.624
Kids, if you get a Happy Meal,

00:01:02.624 --> 00:01:03.925
Joe and George: small,
Harry: Small fries in the paper bag,

00:01:03.925 --> 00:01:04.882
Joe and George: medium,
Harry: medium fries,

00:01:04.882 --> 00:01:06.748
Joe and George: and large.
Harry: and large fries.

00:01:06.748 --> 00:01:08.730
Fries in India come in three sizes,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.040
regular, medium, and large.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.485
The medium and large
come in this really cool

00:01:13.485 --> 00:01:15.210
new packaging where you can just

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.200
open it up like that,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.580
and it's nice and easy to share.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.630
It's a little plate.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.520
Good job, McDonald's. Very innovative.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.020
Harry: So, we couldn't find
the exact weight measurement

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.130
for these fries online,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.047
so what we're going to do
is weigh them ourselves.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.440
Joe: Wow.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.548
Yeah, wow. That worked perfectly,

00:01:32.548 --> 00:01:34.248
that thing I just did
there. Great job, Joe.

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.000
Three exclusive burgers here
in the US are variations

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.370
on the Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.170
Yes, we've all seen "Pulp Fiction."

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.150
We know about the whole
Quarter Pounder thing.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.330
Does not exist outside of
the US, I don't think. So.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.310
The classic Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.360
Look at this guy.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.750
I mean, this was maybe my
go-to one for a decade.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.540
The Quarter Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:58.800
I don't know.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.540
I feel like this is
pretty close to a Whopper.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.980
I'm not a big Whopper guy.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.660
The double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.760
Look at the size of this thing!

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.950
Yes, sir.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:09.960
So, here we've got the
veggie deluxe burger,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.908
which is a veggie burger that's served

00:02:11.908 --> 00:02:13.770
with some mayo and some lettuce.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.780
Here we've got a Chicken Legend,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.030
which is a chicken burger, again,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.650
served with mayo and lettuce.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.540
We have a range of wraps
that you can get in the UK.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.710
We have a wrap of the day.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.120
Here we've got the fajita crisp,

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.820
which is some chicken along with some veg

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.650
and some spicy fajita sauce.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.260
Japan's exclusive burgers.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:36.258
Teriyaki McBurger, which
is my most favorite one.

00:02:36.258 --> 00:02:39.733
My body's made of McTeriyaki Burger.

00:02:42.399 --> 00:02:45.649
[angels singing]

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.410
Bacon lettuce burger right here.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.733
It looks sad.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.300
Egg cheeseburger,

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.210
but we also call it eguchi.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.660
Eguchi is an abbreviation
for "egg cheeseburger."

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.300
Japanese people love abbreviation.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.300
Next one, spicy beef burger.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.800
Ooh, look at this.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.150
Oh, it looks so spicy.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.460
Yeah, spicy mayo or something like that.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.840
So, here, we've got Samurai Mac.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.460
Samurai!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.823
And this blue one is called

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:22.740
roasted soy sauce double thick beef.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.390
We've got roasted soy sauce
bacon tomato thick beef.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:30.290
And this one right here is called

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.498
teriyaki chicken Filet-O.

00:03:32.498 --> 00:03:34.920
Wow. So much sauce.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.920
So, next one, we've got ebi Filet-O.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.310
Ebi means shrimp, so
it's a shrimp Filet-O.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.552
Oh, yeah. It's got aurora sauce.

00:03:43.552 --> 00:03:47.490
Aurora sauce is like
ketchup and mayonnaise.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.732
So, it's got a lot of shrimp in there.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:52.980
Mm.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.020
So good. So good.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.353
Here in India, we can't really

00:03:56.353 --> 00:03:58.530
recreate the iconic McDonald's Big Mac

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.390
because it's made from a beef patty,

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.270
and to keep to the religious
sentiments of Hindus

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.430
and even Muslims, we
don't serve beef or pork

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.960
in a lot of fast-food restaurants.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.950
We have something called
the chicken Maharaja Mac.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:15.000
As you can see, it's got
three buns, two patties,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.583
a lot of cheese, and mayonnaise.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.690
Oh, my God!

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.120
That is truly a Maharaja Mac.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.190
Now let's taste the veg Maharaja Mac.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:28.490
Like, look at this! This is outrageous!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.965
There's no way to eat
this without being messy.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.074
Mm! Oh, my God, that's really good.

00:04:37.074 --> 00:04:41.190
All right, next up is the
iconic McAloo tikki burger.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.070
You take mashed potato, and
you fry it in breadcrumbs,

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.980
and you get this really delicious cutlet.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.263
Mm. It's just so classic.

00:04:49.263 --> 00:04:50.760
They nailed this burger.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.730
Next up, they have a McEgg burger.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.130
McEgg. McEgg, McEgg.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:57.390
I don't know why I did that.

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:58.930
Let's see what that looks like.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.360
Ugh!

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.540
Sorry, I did not expect ... pesto?

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.820
Next up is a chicken kebab burger.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.020
This is not what we're used to seeing

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.070
when we think of kebabs.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.507
The McVeggie, which is
the vegetarian counterpart

00:05:11.507 --> 00:05:13.080
to our McChicken.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.930
If I had to eat this
versus the chicken one,

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.896
I would not be upset at all. Really good.

00:05:18.896 --> 00:05:20.610
We have two "American" burgers.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:23.733
The American Cheese Supreme veg

00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:27.060
and the American Cheese Supreme chicken.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.795
All right, so this is what
the McDonald's website

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.697
says is in this burger.

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:33.540
"Whole-wheat buns
sourced from Maharashtra,

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.120
tangy jalapeños from Karnataka,

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.510
shredded onions grown
in local Indian farms,

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.760
and cheese from Amravati,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.800
also in India."

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:46.740
Quite close to home, this burger.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.350
Currently, this would
probably be my favorite order,

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.820
a McSpicy chicken.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.320
And there's the vegetarian option,

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.100
which is a McSpicy paneer,
which is just leaking lettuce.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.660
For those of you who
don't know what paneer is,

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.670
it's basically cottage cheese.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.903
We love our paneer.

00:06:00.903 --> 00:06:03.900
We put it in curries, we eat
it plain, we put it in kebabs.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.670
It is so delicious.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.890
Fair warning, while this
may have a light kick

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.830
of spice for us, it might
be a hard kick for you,

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.220
so take everything with
a pinch of chili powder.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.130
Every fast-food chain in America right now

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.030
is having what we're calling

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.740
the fried-chicken-sandwich wars.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:23.220
Popeyes, Burger King,
of course McDonald's,

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:25.350
all of them are at this arms race

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:26.610
to have the best chicken sandwich,

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.680
I think 'cause Chick-fil-A
has edged everyone out.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.890
These are the three that
are currently available.

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.540
I don't know for how long.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:34.920
We have the crispy chicken sandwich.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.170
I think this is a brioche bun,

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:38.910
pickles,

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.620
and no sauce, which I think is strange.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.440
Like, the whole flavor
is just the chicken.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.320
Spicy chicken sandwich,

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.650
same deal but, of course,

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.749
spicy sauce!

00:06:51.749 --> 00:06:54.900
And the spicy chicken deluxe,

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.945
which has more vegetables on it.

00:06:56.945 --> 00:06:59.610
You know, to be healthier.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:03.390
Actually, we were supposed
to have bai burger options,

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.630
but unfortunately, you can
only get them from 5:30 p.m.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.030
But let me explain what bai burger is.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.000
Bai simply means double in Japanese.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.040
So if you order a normal Big Mac,

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:15.870
it has two beef patties, right?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.650
But if you order bai Big Mac,
it has four beef patties.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.470
But not only Big Mac, but all burgers

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.840
adopt the bai burger options.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.600
That would not stand
in this country at all.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.700
People would lose their minds.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.360
Four patties at once on a Big Mac?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.760
What we lack in beef
burgers we make up for

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:37.920
in gourmet burgers.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.919
That's right. Here in McDonald's India,

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:41.311
we have our own collection of

00:07:41.311 --> 00:07:44.436
chef's special gourmet burgers.

00:07:44.436 --> 00:07:45.390
Delicious.

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:46.920
And I think this is a rolling menu.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.780
I think they introduce new
things from time to time.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.500
The buns themselves
look a lot more gourmet.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.540
You know, there's a nice
rift down the middle.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.490
Kind of looks like a butt, but that's OK.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.990
We're not gonna concentrate on that.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.710
First up, we have triple
cheese American veg burger

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.650
and triple cheese American chicken burger.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.600
Cheese Lava American veg burger

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.497
and Cheese Lava American chicken burger.

00:08:09.497 --> 00:08:10.721
Again with American,

00:08:10.721 --> 00:08:13.879
and again with the strange relation

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:17.133
of food to volcanoes and lava.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.280
This burger is very spicy.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.490
This qualifies as a
volcano product, for sure.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.380
Congratulations, McDonald's.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.950
The lava in the title
of this burger works.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.230
The McSpicy chicken premium, though,

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.343
has an egg patty inside of it.

00:08:34.343 --> 00:08:36.609
Mm-mm.

00:08:36.609 --> 00:08:39.208
Mm! That's pretty good.

00:08:39.208 --> 00:08:42.360
I just feel so existential right now.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:43.977
Imagine sitting here at this table

00:08:43.977 --> 00:08:47.998
and just tasting every single
burger on a McDonald's menu.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.460
Amazing!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.415
But also, s---.

00:08:52.415 --> 00:08:54.660
We also have some exclusive wrap options.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:57.990
We have Big Spicy paneer
and Big Spicy chicken.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:01.590
I think this is the same
McSpicy chicken patty,

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:04.140
and it's wrapped around a tortilla,

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.420
which is actually way
closer to an Indian chapati

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.980
than most other fast-food restaurants.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.470
It doesn't feel as synthetic.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.870
OK, so when it comes to side menus,

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.693
we've got Shaka Shaka Chicken,

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.360
and we have

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.950
two fla -- oh!

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.300
Two flavors.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.787
Can you hear that?

00:09:22.787 --> 00:09:25.020
Thunder, thunder, thunder.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:27.150
'Cause it's rainy season in Japan.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.240
It's the sunny season here
in southern California.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:32.880
And here is red pepper,

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.058
and this one is cheddar cheese.

00:09:35.058 --> 00:09:38.130
[thundering]

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.847
Thunder, stop!

00:09:39.847 --> 00:09:41.970
So, all we have to do
is just put the powder

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.590
into the bag

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:44.670
and

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:45.931
shake it.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.753
And the powder should
be covering the whole

00:09:52.753 --> 00:09:54.227
Shaka chicken.
[thunder erupts]

00:09:54.227 --> 00:09:56.340
Ooh, big one.

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:57.543
Like this.

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:04.890
We've got side salad,

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:09.030
and it comes with this
roasted sesame dressing.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.350
Let's go!

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.875
Ooh!

00:10:12.875 --> 00:10:14.040
That was cool.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.420
Now put it all in the garbage.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.093
We've got edamame and corn.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.610
Yogurt,

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:23.224
and there is cow.

00:10:23.224 --> 00:10:24.510
Cow.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.100
Here we've got some veggie dippers.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.198
These were actually introduced
as part of Veganuary

00:10:28.198 --> 00:10:29.550
in 2020 in the UK,

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:30.450
but they've stuck on the menu.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:32.520
So these are Vegan Society-approved,

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.790
and they're sort of like a
fried-bean-patty sort of thing.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:38.070
And then, finally, we've
got some mozzarella dippers,

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.470
which are just kind of
mozzarella sticks, really.

00:10:42.026 --> 00:10:44.760
Here in India, we have these add-ons.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:48.240
No. 1, the veg pizza McPuff.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.430
It's basically a pizza Hot Pocket.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:51.720
Masala wedges.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.670
These are potato wedges with

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.370
classic Indian masala flavor to them.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.296
Masalas are basically what we use

00:10:58.296 --> 00:11:00.300
to spice and flavor dishes,

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:02.700
and they consist primarily
of ground-up spices

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:06.690
like cardamom, cloves, red
chilies, Kashmiri chilies.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.090
You go to every Indian home, the mums,

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.790
the grandmums will have their own random

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.950
masala mix that's guarded

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:16.740
and treasured in their family forever.

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.050
Next up, we have cheesy masala wedges.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:23.190
They're also serving a
classic cup of boiled corn,

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:26.723
which is so unique, and they
give you a side of Amul butter.

00:11:26.723 --> 00:11:29.366
Amul butter is part of our culture.

00:11:29.366 --> 00:11:30.750
Makhan.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.190
Makhan!

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.437
This is probably going to be the most

00:11:33.437 --> 00:11:35.154
delicious bite of the day.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:39.540
I love corn.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.890
Next up, chicken strips.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.960
They come in packs of two,

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:44.850
three, or five.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.760
Cheesy nugget veg bites.

