Mm.

00:20:17.573 --> 00:20:19.260
The sausage here in India is not made

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:21.510
out of pork like it is in the US.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:23.902
Instead, it's made out of simple chicken.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:29.530
So, while McDonald's
fries might look and taste

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:31.290
pretty similar in the UK and the US,

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:33.300
in the UK we only have three ingredients,

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:35.373
which is oil, salt, and potatoes.

00:20:37.374 --> 00:20:39.395
The McDonald's french fries in America

00:20:39.395 --> 00:20:40.710
have way more ingredients.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.342
These fries are made
from potatoes, obviously,

00:20:42.342 --> 00:20:44.610
a vegetable oil, which is canola oil,

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.559
corn oil, soybean oil,

00:20:46.559 --> 00:20:48.867
hydrogeni,

00:20:48.867 --> 00:20:50.840
hydrogenitated.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:51.673
Genitated?

00:20:51.673 --> 00:20:52.680
Conner: Hydrogenated.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.030
Ha! Thank you.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:58.260
Hydrogenated soybean oil,
natural beef flavor, dextrose,

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.360
sodium aspid phosphitate?

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:01.685
Phosphifi.

00:21:01.685 --> 00:21:03.102
Phos. Phiupp.

00:21:03.102 --> 00:21:05.587
Pyrophosphate. Pyrophosphate.

00:21:05.587 --> 00:21:07.950
Sodium acid pyrophosphate,

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.230
which is used to maintain the color.

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:11.670
Are they that much of a different color

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:12.750
than the ones in the UK?

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:13.583
Is it worth it?

00:21:13.583 --> 00:21:14.850
Could we get a side-by-side comparison?

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.040
Are they that much more bright yellow

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:19.020
that we need to put
sodium acid pyrophosphate

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.670
or whatever it's called in it?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.690
Salt.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.060
And I should mention that
the natural beef flavor

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:26.130
contains hydrolyzed wheat

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:29.610
and hydrolyzed milk as
a starting ingredient,

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:31.800
and, of course, I have
no idea what that means.

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.900
McDonald's India does
not share a full list

00:21:33.900 --> 00:21:35.070
of their ingredients,

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:38.010
but there are some things
we do know about their food.

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.262
Like, did you know that McDonald's India

00:21:39.262 --> 00:21:41.422
actually changed Indian farming practices

00:21:41.422 --> 00:21:44.100
just so they could grow the
kind of potato that they wanted?

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.470
When they first launched in India in 1996,

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:47.880
McDonald's promised the government

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:49.560
that they would use products grown

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:51.480
and sourced right here in India,

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:53.490
but people who had eaten McDonald's abroad

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:56.580
realized that the fries
didn't taste quite the same.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.230
The reason for this is
that Indian potatoes

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.900
were too small, round,
had way too much moisture

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.130
and sugar content,

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:05.310
and so the fries made out of
them were not long enough,

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.810
they didn't get crispy enough,

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:09.480
and they didn't have that
distinctive McDonald's

00:22:09.480 --> 00:22:10.650
oomph to them.

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.140
So McDonald's partnered with McCain Foods,

00:22:13.140 --> 00:22:16.830
and they spent nine years
trying to perfect their potato.

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:19.680
They imported saplings
which had the perfect shape

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:21.300
and starch content that they needed.

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:23.610
They also chose Gujarat
as their farming location

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:24.600
for its climate,

00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:26.280
and they switched from a flood irrigation

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:29.190
to a sprinkler system to
reduce moisture content

00:22:29.190 --> 00:22:30.600
and save water.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:33.780
The result, bigger and
more starchy potatoes

00:22:33.780 --> 00:22:35.730
that can be used to make
the McDonald's fries

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:37.470
that you know and love.

00:22:37.470 --> 00:22:39.693
So, McDonald's Japan doesn't disclose

00:22:39.693 --> 00:22:41.790
their ingredients in the Big Mac.

00:22:41.790 --> 00:22:46.080
However, they do tell us where
the ingredients come from.

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:48.000
If you order a Big Mac in Japan,

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.870
you'll eat beef from
Australia or New Zealand;

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:53.970
buns made from wheat imported

00:22:53.970 --> 00:22:57.570
from the USA, Canada, and Australia;

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.990
and pickles made from
cucumbers grown in Turkey,

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:03.240
Sri Lanka, or India;

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:06.780
onions grown in the USA or India;

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:10.380
sliced cheddar cheese made
in New Zealand, Australia,

00:23:10.380 --> 00:23:12.690
the USA, or Japan;

00:23:12.690 --> 00:23:14.906
and lettuce grown in Japan,

00:23:14.906 --> 00:23:18.489
Taiwan, the USA, or Malaysia.

00:23:18.489 --> 00:23:21.518
The only ingredients that come from Japan

00:23:21.518 --> 00:23:23.820
are the cheese and the lettuce,

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:26.970
and even then, McDonald's
still imports some lettuce

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.280
and cheese from other countries.

00:23:29.280 --> 00:23:32.163
So this is a very international burger.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:34.639
Thank you, world.

